Hi Josh

So far the occupancy state of species b is only related to the state of occupancy of species A.

  zB[i] ~ dbern(psiB[zA[i] + 1])

  psiB[1] ~ dunif(0, 1) #for sites not occupied by species A (I guess)
  psiB[2] ~ dunif(0, 1) #for sites occupied by species A

You an occupancy probability for sites occupied by A and another for sites not occupied by A.
I guess now you need to link these two probabilities to co-variables similar to what you did with psiA

Please beware that you wrote:
" I'm also assuming that species A does not interfere with the detection of species B"

But what you're coding is not an effect in detection but in occupancy!

In the end I would like to read about this work. Could you send me when you finish?

Cheers

